{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>If you have acted foolishly</b> — before Ithiel and Ukal. <b>Or if you have plotted</b> — put your hand to your mouth and do not speak. Another interpretation: <b>If you have acted foolishly</b> — the word is in past tense in place of future. And the meaning: if you will be a fool, that is, if you commit a folly when you exalt yourself to kingship." "<b>Or if you have plotted</b> — and you planned to commit a folly, put your hand to your mouth and do not carry out the plot. Another interpretation: And if you transgressed by planning to exalt yourself before Him." "<b>Or if you have plotted</b> — put your hand to your mouth." "Another interpretation: <b>If you have acted foolishly</b> — consider in your heart exalting yourself with the help of the Creator." "<b>Or if you have plotted</b> — because of your wickedness, put your hand to your mouth."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:44.508755914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}